From a1a30b3740158dac2e8b226d9b889796705b43f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:10:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm: TF_GLM_SEQ_GROW, every stream's rows on granules of one
 shared pool (default off), TF_GLM_SEQ_GROW_FLOOR_MIB

TF_GLM_SEQ_GROW=1 (default off): each stream's State reserves virtual addresses for the whole window but backs its
row-sized fields (MLA latent rows and int8 scale planes, indexer index keys) with VMM granules only up to the rows its passes
reach (State.ready), plus a 4,096-row margin. The granules come from one pool made at startup with exactly the granules one
whole-window State needs, so a lone stream still reaches the full window and several streams decode together while their rows
fit the pool together. Kernels and layouts are unchanged (same contiguous addresses; mapped granules are zeroed as the whole-window
arena was), so the bytes are the same with the switch on or off. Admission (rank 0 lanes) charges granules (LaneMemory requeues);
TF_GLM_SEQ_GROW_STREAMS (1..16, default 4) caps the streams and every rank checks at startup that its MemAvailable holds the
further streams' fixed parts above a floor (one startup all-gather: the ranks agree on the switch, the cap and the floor, and every one must fit, or all refuse).

TF_GLM_SEQ_GROW_FLOOR_MIB (new here, 2304..65535, default 3072 = the floor as before): the floor of that check. EXLR8 up1 on TP4
leaves a rank 2.7-3.1 GiB of MemAvailable at idle (spark1 min 2.74 GiB), under the default 3 GiB + (streams - 1) x ~48 MiB; the
variable lowers the check (never below MEMGUARD's 2 GiB + 256 MiB). The floor travels in the agreement word, so ranks that read different floors refuse. Memory admission only, no kernel or byte changes.

Tests: test-glm-seq-grow-host (granules follow rows, trims, shared pool, refusal, the stream cap, the floor) and
test-glm-seq-grow-gpu (TF_SEQ_GROW_GPU=1, a device: mapped zeroed, kept across trims, refused when spent).
Rebased from x6-conc 0203 (K4, passed x6g/x7) onto 0001-0195 + 0205-0209.
